flowchart TB
  accTitle: The support review assistant and its approval boundary
  accDescr: Read demo order details, propose a case, persist a pause and await the human decision. Approval writes a deduplicated case to SQLite. A declined action does not write to the review queue.
  inspect["1 · INSPECT\nRead the order and its recorded facts"]
  propose["2 · PROPOSE\nOrder id + reason for review"]
  pause[("3 · PAUSE DURABLY\nShow the exact proposed arguments")]
  decision{"Human decision"}
  queue["4 · APPROVE\nQueue a case with a stable operation id"]
  decline["DECLINE\nLeave the review queue unchanged"]
  finish["5 · REPORT\nReturn the actual case id and status"]
  inspect --> propose --> pause --> decision
  decision -->|approved| queue --> finish
  decision -->|declined| decline
  classDef main fill:#ddf4e9,color:#133c36,stroke:#228063,stroke-width:2px;
  classDef amber fill:#fff5df,color:#634919,stroke:#bf9652;
  classDef muted fill:#f2f5f8,color:#263746,stroke:#a2b1bf;
  class inspect,queue,finish main;
  class pause,decision amber;
  class propose,decline muted;
